content.text:
render: Render your working recipe after applying `patch`, or render a whole new `recipe` (one or the other). Returns validation errors, or every frame (up to 16) cropped to the effect and enlarged 2x (3x when small) on a checker, each layer's frames and peak, where the subject landed and warnings that name the layer; the result becomes your working recipe. frames=[...] shows just those frames (1-based); zoom=N (1-8) shows them bigger. check_controls=true adds every slider/toggle at min / current / max on a frame where it shows, and flags any that change nothing. fit_canvas=true first resizes the canvas to the effect + a 3 px margin (use it when things are cut off or float in empty space). patch = list of ops applied in order to your working recipe ([] renders it as is): {"op": "set", "path": "layers.circle.radius", "value": 40} (any path: layers.<id>.<field>[.from|.keys.1.1], controls.<id>.value, camera.tilt, ramps.main, frames ...); {"op": "remove", "path": "layers.sparks.wobble"}; {"op": "add_layer", "layer": {...}, "after": "<id>"} (or "before"; default: on top); {"op": "replace_layer", "layer": {...}}; {"op": "remove_layer", "id": "<id>"}; {"op": "add_control", "control": {...}}; {"op": "replace_control", "control": {...}}; {"op": "remove_control", "id": "<id>"}; {"op": "remove_group", "group": "<name>"} (every layer with that group, and their sliders); {"op": "retime", "frames": N, "keep": "duration"|"speed"} (duration: fps follows; life windows land on frames) or {"op": "retime", "lead_in": k} (k frames before everything, one-shots); {"op": "scale", "factor": 0.5, "about": [x, y]} (positions, radii, widths, speeds and their sliders; about defaults to the origin; the sprite keeps its size); {"op": "move", "group": "<name>", "by": [dx, dy]} (a group's positions and the sliders that write them). A set on a value a control writes moves that control instead.
arguments (one JSON object; required: none):
- patch: array (shape: describe edits)
- recipe: object (shape: describe recipe)
- check_controls: {"type": "boolean"}
- fit_canvas: {"type": "boolean"}
- frames: {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1}}
- zoom: {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 8}
call: vfx_workbench(argv=['<step id>', 'render', '{...}'])

review before your next call: say what you see in the frames — does it read at 1x, start -> peak -> end (or a loop with no jump), anything cut off at the edges, muddy colours, is the sprite still readable — then choose: set_part or render with a patch (a defect you saw), get_part (unsure what a part can do), or export. Put that reasoning in `notes`.
